In article <1993Jun21.202634.23551@ultb.isc.rit.edu>, kdc5072@ultb.isc.rit.edu (K.D. Colagio) writes...
> I have, in my NETHACKOPTIONS environment variable, this:
>    pickup,pickup_types:$
> but when I start nethack, it shows the pickup_types to be set to all...

     That should be  autopickup,pickup_types:$

> Anyone either 1) know why, 2) have this problem, 3) know what to do
> about it???

     Options end up getting processed right to left.  The pickup without
any value is treated as `autopickup,pickup_types:all' for backwards
compatibility, thereby immediately replacing the `pickup_types:$' that
you'd just set.



